The follow-up commit for after ecto/vcad#867 merges to main.

  git apply docs/after-vcad-867.patch

RE-CHECK THE SHA BEFORE APPLYING. The vcad rev below is origin/main as of
2026-09-09 (git -C ../vcad ls-remote origin main → e9697505b1e0dbd329089b60
b645daa6626570bf). If #867 landed after that, or main moved, run ls-remote
again and use the merge commit instead of this one.

What it does:
  - bumps every vcad git dep to that main rev (which tracks kosm-render 0.2)
  - kosm-render 0.1.1 → 0.2.0, and its in-workspace consumers to "0.2"
  - deletes [patch."https://github.com/ecto/kosm"], which only existed to
    close the back-edge while vcad pinned an old kosm-render

After applying: drop the "held at 0.1.x" paragraph from
crates/kosm-render/Cargo.toml, run `cargo metadata` and confirm only ONE
kosm-render is in the graph, then tag kosm-render-v0.2.0.

